Company Information

	Companies are the body of the game Assassin.  They rule the world!
All players are signed onto a company when they first start.  They not only
supply the assassin with missions (such as 'kill this CEO'), they give high
rewards and experience for completed COMPANY ONLY missions.

	The goal of each player is to make his company on top, no matter
how he does it.  At the initializing of the game, each company has the same
amount of FUNDS and executives, your goal is to either force the companies
bankrupt or kill off all the executives in the other companies.

	When an assassin kills the last executive of a company, his company
will get 90% of the killed companies' funds, with the assassin recieving
10%, no more than $100,000.  All assassins belonging to the killed company
will be reset!

	Assassins may belong to the same company, however if an assassin
fights and kills another assassin of the same company, that company will 
send out an 'internal hit', where they will be hunted down and killed once!
Other penalties for attacking a fellow company employee will be a deduction
of 50% of your bank funds, loss of experience, deduction of charisma or 
others.

	When all other companies are destroyed, the users will fight each
other until the maximum level is achieved, and the SysOp will reset the game
when needed, however when the SysOp resets the game,  the person with the 
greatest experience will NOT be reset, only until he is defeated by another 
human or computer person!  When this happens the dead person will be reset,
and the next experienced assassin will take over as the leader.

	Last, when you join a company you sign a waiver stating if you
quit you will lose 50% of your bank funds, no less than $10000.  You need 
more than $20000 in the bank to quit a company.  
